<!-- Logo master: construction guide only. It holds no mark on purpose: every direction starts from
     its own idea (references/logo-principles.md), never from a shared placeholder shape.
     Copy it to brand/mark.svg (or a direction file) and replace {{BRAND}} and {{MARK_GEOMETRY}}.
     export_svg.py refuses a file that still holds a {{...}} placeholder.
     Construction:
     - 1024 x 1024 viewBox. Keep the mark inside the 820 x 820 live area (x/y 102-922): about 10%
       clear space on every side, which launcher masks and the app-icon tile need.
     - Centre optically, not mathematically: heavy-bottomed and pointed shapes usually sit a little
       above the geometric centre. Check it at 32 px and inside a circle mask.
     - Flat shapes filled from the brand colour tokens (brand/tokens.json). No text inside the mark,
       no raster images, no filters, no effect the mark depends on (export and masks mangle them).
     - Keep a mono variant (one fill) and a reverse variant (for dark backgrounds) alongside it. -->
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" width="1024" height="1024">
  <title>{{BRAND}} mark</title>
  {{MARK_GEOMETRY}}
</svg>
